From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: 988 - fire topology rebuild on agent count

topology_build_tree() (which writes topology_link, the source of truth for
depth/upstream) only runs when num_agents == topology_num_devs(). But
num_agents excludes the colocated controller root while topology_num_devs()
includes it, so the two sides count different populations. Once a 2-hop agent
joined, the root stayed in the dev list and the counts never matched again,
so the tree was never rebuilt and topology_link froze at the first hop
(x8->8g second hop missing, x8 depth=-1, controller depth=-1).

Add topology_num_agent_devs() (devs excluding the root) and gate on it, so the
rebuild fires once every agent has reported regardless of the colocated-agent
marked/unmarked flap. depth then flows from tdev->bh.depth and the multi-hop
edges from the BFS walk.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/topology.c
+++ b/src/topology.c
@@ -50,6 +50,20 @@
 	return topology->num_devs;
 }
 
+uint32_t topology_num_agent_devs(struct bh_topology_data *topology,
+				 const uint8_t *root_almac)
+{
+	struct bh_topology_dev *bh_topo_dev = NULL;
+	uint32_t n = 0;
+
+	list_for_each_entry(bh_topo_dev, &topology->dev_list, list) {
+		if (!hwaddr_equal(bh_topo_dev->al_macaddr, root_almac))
+			n++;
+	}
+
+	return n;
+}
+
 struct bh_topology_dev *topology_find_device(struct bh_topology_data *topology, const uint8_t *al_macaddr)
 {
 	struct bh_topology_dev *bh_topo_dev = NULL;
--- a/src/topology.h
+++ b/src/topology.h
@@ -82,6 +82,8 @@
 
 /** Number of devices in backhaul topology tree. */
 uint32_t topology_num_devs(struct bh_topology_data *topology);
+uint32_t topology_num_agent_devs(struct bh_topology_data *topology,
+				 const uint8_t *root_almac);
 
 /** Returns backhaul topology device if exists in the model, NULL otherwise. */
 struct bh_topology_dev *topology_find_device(struct bh_topology_data *topology, const uint8_t *al_macaddr);
--- a/src/cntlr_map.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_map.c
@@ -800,12 +800,19 @@
 	if (!is_topology_valid(&c->topology)) {
 		bool standalone = cntlr_is_standalone(c);
 
-		if (standalone)
-			topology_remove_device(&c->topology, c->almacaddr);
-
-		if (c->num_agents == topology_num_devs(&c->topology)) {
-			if (standalone)
+		/* Gate on agents only. num_agents excludes the colocated controller
+		 * root, but topology_num_devs() includes it, so the old
+		 * num_agents == topology_num_devs() compared two different
+		 * populations and stopped firing once a 2-hop agent joined (root
+		 * present => counts differ), freezing topology_link at the first
+		 * hop. Count agent devs on both sides so the rebuild fires once
+		 * every agent has reported, regardless of the colocated-agent flap. */
+		if (c->num_agents ==
+		    topology_num_agent_devs(&c->topology, c->almacaddr)) {
+			if (standalone) {
+				topology_remove_device(&c->topology, c->almacaddr);
 				build_local_controller_root(c, &c->topology, c->almacaddr);
+			}
 
 			topology_build_tree(c, &c->topology, c->almacaddr);
 
